Aura licensing

Aurora Silicon contributions are licensed under GNU GPL version 2 only
(GPL-2.0-only). This includes the authorized Aurora contributions carried
into this repository and all new Aura contributions.

Inherited m1n1 code remains MIT licensed. Its original notice and full terms
are preserved in LICENSES/MIT.txt. Third-party components keep their own
licences and notices in 3rdparty_licenses and their source directories.

A file containing inherited MIT code and Aurora contributions is marked
MIT AND GPL-2.0-only: MIT applies to the inherited portions and GPL-2.0-only
to the Aurora portions. This does not offer the Aurora portions under MIT.
Authorship and change boundaries remain recorded in the full Git history.

See LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt for the full GPLv2 text and docs/licensing.md
for provenance and contribution policy. Historical copies retain the terms
under which they were originally distributed. Logo and font terms remain
separate from the source-code licences.
